      "message": "policy: reject invalid CFeeRate values when deserializing\n\nCFeeRate constructors turn a non-positive size into the empty feerate\n{0, 0}, but Unserialize read fee and size from the stream unchecked.\nA negative size then reaches FeeFrac::EvaluateFee, which requires a\npositive size: debug builds hit an Assume failure, and release builds\ncompute wrong fees. A zero size with a nonzero fee compares as an\ninfinite feerate.\n\nNothing deserializes a CFeeRate on master, but the UnstableChain IPC\ninterface in #29409, used by the multiprocess wallet in #10102, passes\nfeerates as serialized Data fields, so an IPC client could send these\nvalues.\n\nThrow on values the constructors cannot produce, like other\ndeserialization errors.\n\nThis issue was found by Project Loupe and passed on by Greg Sanders.\n\nThis change was written with Claude Opus 5.5.",
      "committer": {
        "name": "Ryan Ofsky",
        "email": "ryan@ofsky.org",
        "date": "2026-11-09T15:51:03Z"
